#!/usr/bin/env python3
# tribes-server -- headless dedicated-server host + updater for the Modern Tribes repack.
#
# Linux-first, command line only, Python 3.8+ standard library only. Runs the Windows
# server exe (ModernTribes.exe -dedicated) under Wine with no display, supervises it
# (crash restart, crash-loop breaker, hang detection), gives it a console you can type
# into from any shell, and keeps the install current from the SAME manifest the in-game
# updater reads -- no client launch needed.
#
#   python3 tribes-server install ~/tribes      first install (server-only file set)
#   ./tribes-server config                      write/show server.ini
#   ./tribes-server run                         foreground (systemd / docker / tmux)
#   ./tribes-server start | stop | restart | status | logs -f
#   ./tribes-server tui                         full-screen terminal UI (console, players, maps,
#                                               settings, store) -- closing it never stops the server
#   ./tribes-server console ["say(0, \"hi\");"] send a command, or attach interactively
#   ./tribes-server update [--check]            delta-update (stops/restarts if running)
#   ./tribes-server systemd                     print a systemd unit for this install
#   ./tribes-server doctor                      check wine, disk, ports, files
#
# Mirrors, deliberately and by name, the Windows pieces it replaces:
#   updater.cpp      manifest format, https-only fetch, sha256 verify, staging in _update\,
#                    updver.txt, SEED-ONLY files (updSeedOnly), devtree.txt guard, channel.txt
#   hostgui.cpp      profiles, -nomodlist launch line, config\hostgui.cs writer
#                    (writeHostguiCs), rpgserv.cs/rmrpgserv.cs surgical edit, crash-loop rule,
#                    GameSpyQuery1 (0x62) status probe
# Keep them in step: a change to one of those rules belongs here too.

